framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0026:
  description |
    Correct the Compact V2 psyche prompt contract and allow one bounded
    semantic-closure repair after an application schema rejection.

problem P1:
  |
    Structured provider output is not perfectly reliable. The first real
    Compact V2 replay returned a complete object with six empty appraisal
    strings that the consumer schema rejects. Regenerating the whole stage is
    wasteful, but repairing only reported error paths can leave fields that
    passed validation semantically inconsistent with the correction.

premise DRIVER_SOURCE:
  |
    Correct the producing contract before adding containment. The producer
    prompt and consumer schema must express the same non-empty requirements.

premise DRIVER_COHERENCE:
  |
    A repair scope is the smallest server-defined semantic dependency closure,
    not merely the validator error paths and not a scope chosen freely by the
    model. The merged full result remains the acceptance subject.

premise DRIVER_BOUND:
  |
    The server owns repair eligibility, writable roots, merge behavior, full
    revalidation, provider accounting, and the one-attempt limit. Failed repair
    fails closed and is never recursively repaired.

premise DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    ADR-0025 remains authoritative for expression-state/history separation,
    nextUtterance acceptance, exact-repetition validity, and the existing battle
    revision commit boundary. A repair is not a critic, similarity classifier,
    fallback utterance, or second commit lifecycle.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered options are: fail every schema-invalid first result; regenerate
    the complete psyche output; patch only reported paths; let the model choose
    arbitrary affected paths; or replace one server-defined semantic closure and
    revalidate the merged full result. The last option preserves unrelated valid
    state while allowing necessary dependent values to change.

evidence E_SCHEMA:
  |
    CharacterDeepPsycheCompactAdvanceSchema requires six non-empty appraisal
    strings and enforces continuityBasis.kind from continuityDecision.
    CharacterExpressionBrief repeats continuityDecision and carries the focus,
    observed impact, relationship move, and public aim derived from that same
    appraisal.

evidence E_PROMPT:
  |
    The current generation prompt describes required appraisal semantics but its
    concrete return example renders all six schema-required strings as empty and
    does not state the non-empty constraint at the return boundary.

evidence E_REPLAY:
  |
    The 2026-09-09 grok-4.3 response copied all six empty values, filled other
    parts of the structure, and failed with too_small. It completed JSON using
    191 of 1200 output tokens, so truncation is not a credible primary cause.

evidence E_RCA:
  |
    The command-line LLMThink RCA audit completed with no findings. It identifies
    prompt/schema mismatch as the integration root cause, hand-authored valid
    fixtures as the escape cause, and the model's hidden selection mechanism as
    unknown. The separate Grok retrospective is supporting hypothesis only.

evidence E_PRECEDENT:
  |
    Character-definition generation already uses one bounded application repair
    with validation issues followed by the same strict schema and fail-closed
    behavior. Compact psyche currently has transport retry only and no equivalent
    application repair.

evidence E_OWNER_DIRECTION:
  |
    On 2026-09-09 the product owner directed correction in this direction and
    clarified that the patch must remain minimal but may update fields that had
    passed schema validation when required for semantic consistency.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_SOURCE, E_PROMPT, E_REPLAY, E_RCA:
  |
    Align the initial Compact V2 deep-psyche producer prompt with the accepted
    schema. State immediately before the return contract that the six appraisal
    strings are non-empty, replace empty-string exemplars with semantic value
    markers that cannot be copied as accepted empty values, and keep the schema
    strict rather than weakening it.

decision D2 based_on P1, DRIVER_COHERENCE, E_SCHEMA, OPTIONS:
  |
    When the first decoded Compact V2 deep-psyche candidate fails application
    schema validation within the appraisal/expression semantic group, permit one
    repair response containing complete replacements for speechAppraisal and
    expressionBrief. It may additionally replace complete dialogueThread,
    observableManifestations, or narrativeCues values only when the correction
    changes their meaning. It cannot change other delta fields.

decision D3 based_on D2, DRIVER_COHERENCE, DRIVER_BOUND:
  |
    The repair request contains the rejected semantic slice, machine-readable
    validation issues, a deterministic description of the violated contract,
    relevant immutable observation and dialogue context, and the exact writable
    roots. The model returns only the closed repair envelope. The server rejects
    unexpected roots, merges allowed replacements into the preserved decoded
    candidate, and runs the normal decoder, complete schema, and all cross-field
    refinements over the merged result.

decision D4 based_on D2, D3, DRIVER_BOUND, E_PRECEDENT:
  |
    Allow at most one application repair per logical Compact psyche result. Use
    a distinct provider-operation label, lower temperature, normal physical-call
    accounting, and retain both attempts in observation evidence. Do not repair
    a non-object root, an error outside the declared semantic group, or a failed
    repair. Those cases keep the current fail-closed behavior. Provider transport
    retries remain separate and do not reset the application-repair limit.

decision D5 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    Preserve the normal one-call successful path and every ADR-0025 state,
    history, expression, repetition, and commit invariant. The repair does not
    weaken validation, fabricate a fallback result, change an existing battle's
    bound dialogue contract, or authorize a paid replay, deployment, or release.

decision D6 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5:
  |
    Verification must cover no repair on valid first output; exact repair input
    and writable roots; dependent fields allowed despite prior field validity;
    rejection of unauthorized roots; merge into preserved unrelated fields;
    complete revalidation; one-repair maximum; failed-repair closure; distinct
    provider accounting; and unchanged legacy and normal Compact behavior.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-09, after the ADR overview, repair flow, semantic closure,
    boundaries, and tradeoffs were explained, the product owner replied,
    "OKです。承認します。" The approved pre-acceptance .think snapshot had
    SHA-256 5a6297a8cf3dbb44422c3a09d0aa27615edbdaff359f0c7c91fc77bb2da90c93.

evidence NAMESPACE_RECONCILIATION:
  |
    Fresh integration readback on 2026-09-09 established that current main had
    already accepted ADR-0024 for detached authoring and allocated ADR-0025 to
    the prerequisite Compact expression-state decision. This dependent repair
    decision was therefore allocated ADR-0026. Its approved decision content
    and acceptance digest are unchanged.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, NAMESPACE_RECONCILIATION:
  |
    ADR-0026 retains Accepted status for this owner-approved revision. Local
    implementation of D1 through D6 is authorized. The identifier change only
    reconciles the mainline namespace. Paid provider replay, deployment,
    release, and changes outside the Compact V2 deep-psyche repair boundary
    remain separate actions requiring their own authority.

evidence E_IMPLEMENTATION_20260909:
  |
    The local implementation aligns the Compact V2 producer contract, adds a
    closed one-attempt semantic-closure repair, merges only server-declared
    roots, and revalidates the complete result. Provider-operation taxonomy v2
    accounts for the repair as deepPsyche and observation projection reserves
    the possible extra physical attempt. Focused tests, the full test suite,
    typecheck, build, duplicate detection, and the pinned Lizard complexity gate
    completed successfully before final readback. No paid provider replay,
    deployment, or release was performed by this implementation.

decision IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS based_on ACCEPTANCE, E_IMPLEMENTATION_20260909:
  |
    D1 through D6 are implemented locally. Existing observation runs remain
    bound to their recorded taxonomy revision; they are not reinterpreted or
    resumed under taxonomy v2. A future provider replay or deployment remains a
    separately authorized action.
